    # 🎯 Linux Pro Tip #1
    
    One of the most valuable habits you can build is **reading the documentation instead of searching the web for every command**.
    
    For example, if you forget how to use `find`, don't immediately search Google. Try:
    
    ```bash
    man find
    ```
    
    or:
    
    ```bash
    find --help
    ```
    
    This habit will make you more independent and much faster at learning Linux.
    
